module

public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSaturation.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSaturation.Quotient
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.GradedAlgebra.AssociatedPrimesHomogeneous

/-!
# `I(V₊(I))` for a graded ring that is not generated in degree one

Let `A = ⨁_{n ≥ 0} 𝒜 n` be a Noetherian graded ring, let `g : ι → A` be a finite family of
homogeneous generators of `A` over `𝒜 0`, of positive degrees `e j`, and let

`d = lcm (e j)`.

Stacks tag 0BXK answers, for a homogeneous ideal `I ⊆ A` and the closed subscheme
`V₊(I) = Proj (𝒜 ⧸ I)` of Constructions tag 01N0,

`I(V₊(I)) = {x ∈ A | 𝒜 (n · d) · x ⊆ I for all n ≫ 0}`.

That is the clause proved here. The condition is on the **multiples of `x` by the elements of the
homogeneous component `𝒜 (n · d)`**, for every sufficiently large `n` — not on the degree-`n · d`
component of the ideal `A x`, which is the shape the published text has and which is
false; the ring of `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/ProjSaturation/WeightedExample.lean`
separates the two.

## Which `I(V₊(I))`

`I(Z) = Ker(A ⟶ ⨁_{n ≥ 0} Γ(Z, 𝒪_Z(n)))`, and for `Z = V₊(I) = Proj (𝒜 ⧸ I)` the sheaves
`𝒪_Z(n)` here are the **twisting sheaves of `Proj (𝒜 ⧸ I)` itself** — the reading
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/ProjSaturation/Quotient.lean` takes for the degree-one clause of
the same tag, and the reading in which the source derives this clause, by applying Cohomology of
Schemes tag 0BXF to the ring `A ⧸ I`. So the kernel is spelled as it is there: an element of `A`
lies in `I(V₊(I))` when the twisted section on `Proj (𝒜 ⧸ I)` attached to the class of each of
its homogeneous components vanishes.

The other reading — the sections of `𝒪_{Proj 𝒜}(n)` *pulled back* along `V₊(I) ⟶ Proj 𝒜`, which
is what `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.idealOfClosedSubscheme` is defined by and what
the degree-one clause of this tag is registered on in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/ProjSaturation/VPlus.lean` — is **not** the one in which this
clause holds, and the formula above is false for it. Take the ring of `WeightedExample.lean`,
`A = ℚ[x, y]` with `deg x = 2` and `deg y = 3`, so `d = 6`, and take `I = (y)`. Then `y` lies in
the right-hand side for a trivial reason, `𝒜 (6n) · y ⊆ (y)`; but the pullback of its section of
`𝒪(3)` to `V₊(y)` is nonzero, because `(A[1/x])₃ = (y / 1) · ℚ[y² / x³]` is free of rank one on
`y / 1` itself — so `𝒪(3)` is trivialized by the canonical section of `y`, i.e. that section is
nowhere vanishing — while `V₊(y) = Proj ℚ[x]` is a nonempty reduced point of `D₊(x)`, and a
nowhere-vanishing section does not pull back to zero on a nonempty closed subscheme. The chart
computation is the one recorded in the module docstring of `WeightedExample.lean`. In the same
example the pullback reading does not even give `I ⊆ I(V₊(I))`.

The two readings differ only because the comparison map `(Proj.map ψ)^* 𝒪_{Proj 𝒜}(n) ⟶
𝒪_{Proj (𝒜 ⧸ I)}(n)` of tag 01N0 part (3) need not be injective. When `A` is generated by `𝒜 1`
over `𝒜 0` — the hypothesis of the degree-one clause — every degree is a multiple of `d = 1`,
every twist is invertible, and the question does not arise.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.mem_irrelevant_pow_of_mem_of_mul_le`: a homogeneous
  element of degree at least `N · d` lies in the `N`-th power of the irrelevant ideal. This is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.mem_irrelevant_pow_of_mem` with generation in degree
  one relaxed to generation by a family of degrees dividing `d`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.degreeSection_eq_zero_iff_forall_mul_eq_zero`: **the
  vanishing criterion for a twisted section at a general degree** — the section of `b` on
  `Proj 𝒜` vanishes exactly when `𝒜 (n · d) · b = 0` for all `n ≫ 0`. This is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.degreeSection_eq_zero_iff` with generation in degree
  one relaxed in the same way.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj`
  `.degreeSection_quotientGradingMk_eq_zero_iff_forall_mul_mem`: the same for the class of a
  homogeneous element of `A` on `V₊(I)`, elementwise in each degree.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj`
  `.forall_degreeSection_quotientGradingMk_eq_zero_iff` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj`
  `.setOf_forall_degreeSection_quotientGradingMk_eq_zero`: **the clause**,
  `I(V₊(I)) = {x ∈ A | 𝒜 (n · d) x ⊆ I for all n ≫ 0}` with `d` the least common multiple of the
  degrees of the generators, elementwise and as an equality of sets.

## Implementation notes

Two things in the degree-one argument of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/ProjSaturation/Basic.lean` are about degree one and not about
charts, and both are generalized there rather than redone here: that the twisted section of `b`
restricted to `D₊(f)` is the fraction `b / f ^ 0`, whose vanishing says a power of `f` kills `b`
(`exists_pow_mul_eq_zero_of_degreeSection_eq_zero'` — the associated-module-sheaf description
asks only that `deg f` be positive, and in particular does not ask `𝒪(n)` to be invertible, which
for `n` not a multiple of `d` it is not), and the converse chartwise criterion
(`degreeSection_eq_zero_of_forall_exists_pow_mul_eq_zero`, which takes any cover by standard
opens of positive-degree elements; Mathlib's `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.iSup_basicOpen_eq_top'`
supplies one from the generators).

What is left is the passage between "each generator has a power killing `b`" and "`𝒜 (n · d)`
kills `b` for all `n ≫ 0`". Forwards: the generators span the irrelevant ideal
(`generates_algebra_iff_generates_irrelevant`, tag 07Z4, which is already stated for generators
of arbitrary positive degrees), so that ideal lies in the radical of the annihilator of `b`, a
finitely generated ideal inside a radical has a power inside the ideal
(`Ideal.exists_pow_le_of_le_radical_of_fg`, the one place Noetherianness is used), and
`mem_irrelevant_pow_of_mem_of_mul_le` puts every element of `𝒜 (n · d)` with `n ≥ N` into the
`N`-th power. Backwards: `g j ^ (n · d / e j)` lies in `𝒜 (n · d)`, which is where `e j ∣ d` is
needed and is the whole reason `d` is a common multiple of the degrees.

`mem_irrelevant_pow_of_mem_of_mul_le` is the only genuinely new induction. For a single degree
`e j`, a homogeneous element of degree `m > 0` is a sum of multiples of the generators, and
taking degree-`m` components makes the cofactor of `g j` homogeneous of degree `m - e j`; since
`e j ≤ d`, an element of degree at least `(N + 1) · d` has all its cofactors of degree at least
`N · d`. Degree one is the case `e ≡ 1`, `d = 1`, where this reads `𝒜 m ⊆ 𝒜₊ ^ m`.

The statements are given for an arbitrary common multiple `d` of the degrees, and the two
carrying the tag are then stated at `d = Finset.univ.lcm e`, which is what the source names.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BXK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BXK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BXF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BXF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07Z4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07Z4)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01N0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N0)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open DirectSum

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj

open Stacks.HomogeneousIdeal

universe u w

variable {S : Type u} {σ : Type w} [CommRing S] [SetLike σ S] [AddSubgroupClass σ S]
  (𝒮 : ℕ → σ) [GradedRing 𝒮]

/-! ### Homogeneous elements of large degree lie in powers of the irrelevant ideal -/

/-- **A homogeneous element of degree at least `N · d` lies in the `N`-th power of the irrelevant
ideal**, when `S` is generated over `𝒮 0` by homogeneous elements whose degrees divide `d`.

This is `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.mem_irrelevant_pow_of_mem`, which is the case
of generators of degree one and `d = 1`, with the degrees allowed to be any positive divisors of
`d`. The induction is the same: a homogeneous element of positive degree `m` is a sum of
multiples of the generators, and taking degree-`m` components leaves the cofactor of `g j`
homogeneous of degree `m - e j ≥ N · d`, because `e j ≤ d`. -/
theorem mem_irrelevant_pow_of_mem_of_mul_le {ι : Type*} (g : ι → S) (e : ι → ℕ)
    (he : ∀ j, 0 < e j) (hg : ∀ j, g j ∈ 𝒮 (e j))
    (hgen : Algebra.adjoin (𝒮 0) (Set.range g) = ⊤) {d : ℕ} (hd : 0 < d)
    (hdvd : ∀ j, e j ∣ d) (N : ℕ) :
    ∀ m : ℕ, N * d ≤ m → ∀ x : S, x ∈ 𝒮 m →
      x ∈ (HomogeneousIdeal.irrelevant 𝒮).toIdeal ^ N := by
  have hspan : Ideal.span (Set.range g) = (HomogeneousIdeal.irrelevant 𝒮).toIdeal :=
    (generates_algebra_iff_generates_irrelevant 𝒮 g e he hg).mp hgen
  induction N with
  | zero => intro m _ x _; simp
  | succ N ih =>
      intro m hm x hx
      rw [add_one_mul] at hm
      have hdm : d ≤ m := (Nat.le_add_left d (N * d)).trans hm
      have hm0 : 0 < m := hd.trans_le hdm
      have hxspan : x ∈ Ideal.span (Set.range g) := by
        rw [hspan]
        exact mem_irrelevant_of_mem_of_pos 𝒮 hx hm0
      obtain ⟨k, c, gg, hsum⟩ := Submodule.mem_span_set'.mp hxspan
      rw [← proj_eq_self_of_mem 𝒮 hx, ← hsum, map_sum]
      simp only [smul_eq_mul]
      rw [pow_succ]
      refine Ideal.sum_mem _ fun i _ ↦ ?_
      obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ := (gg i).2
      have hejd : e j ≤ d := Nat.le_of_dvd hd (hdvd j)
      rw [← hj, proj_mul_eq 𝒮 (c i) (g j) (e j) m (hg j) (hejd.trans hdm)]
      exact Ideal.mul_mem_mul
        (ih (m - e j) (Nat.le_sub_of_add_le (le_trans (Nat.add_le_add_left hejd (N * d)) hm)) _
          (proj_mem 𝒮 (c i) (m - e j)))
        (mem_irrelevant_of_mem_of_pos 𝒮 (hg j) (he j))

/-! ### The vanishing criterion for a twisted section at a general degree -/

/-- **If the twisted section of `b` on `Proj 𝒮` vanishes, then `𝒮 (n · d)` annihilates `b` for
every `n ≫ 0`.** Each generator has a power killing `b`, so the irrelevant ideal — which the
generators span — lies in the radical of the annihilator of `b`; being finitely generated it then
has a power inside the annihilator, and every element of `𝒮 (n · d)` with `n ≥ N` lies in the
`N`-th power. -/
theorem exists_forall_mul_eq_zero_of_degreeSection_eq_zero [IsNoetherianRing S] {ι : Type*}
    (g : ι → S) (e : ι → ℕ) (he : ∀ j, 0 < e j) (hg : ∀ j, g j ∈ 𝒮 (e j))
    (hgen : Algebra.adjoin (𝒮 0) (Set.range g) = ⊤) {d : ℕ} (hd : 0 < d)
    (hdvd : ∀ j, e j ∣ d) {n : ℕ} (b : 𝒮 n) (hb : degreeSection 𝒮 n b = 0) :
    ∃ N : ℕ, ∀ m : ℕ, N ≤ m → ∀ y : S, y ∈ 𝒮 (m * d) → y * (b : S) = 0 := by
  set K := (Submodule.span S ({(b : S)} : Set S)).annihilator
  have hJrad : (HomogeneousIdeal.irrelevant 𝒮).toIdeal ≤ K.radical := by
    rw [← (generates_algebra_iff_generates_irrelevant 𝒮 g e he hg).mp hgen, Ideal.span_le]
    rintro _ ⟨j, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := exists_pow_mul_eq_zero_of_degreeSection_eq_zero' 𝒮 b hb (hg j) (he j)
    rw [SetLike.mem_coe, Ideal.mem_radical_iff]
    exact ⟨t, (Submodule.mem_annihilator_span_singleton (b : S) (g j ^ t)).mpr
      (by simpa [smul_eq_mul] using ht)⟩
  obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ :=
    Ideal.exists_pow_le_of_le_radical_of_fg hJrad (Ideal.fg_of_isNoetherianRing _)
  refine ⟨N, fun m hm y hy ↦ ?_⟩
  have hmem := hN (mem_irrelevant_pow_of_mem_of_mul_le 𝒮 g e he hg hgen hd hdvd N (m * d)
    (Nat.mul_le_mul_right d hm) y hy)
  simpa [smul_eq_mul] using (Submodule.mem_annihilator_span_singleton (b : S) y).mp hmem

/-- **If `𝒮 (n · d)` annihilates `b` for every `n ≫ 0`, the twisted section of `b` vanishes.**
The standard opens of the generators cover `Proj 𝒮`, and `g j ^ (N · d / e j)` is an element of
`𝒮 (N · d)` killing `b`, so the section dies on every chart. -/
theorem degreeSection_eq_zero_of_forall_mul_eq_zero {ι : Type*} (g : ι → S) (e : ι → ℕ)
    (he : ∀ j, 0 < e j) (hg : ∀ j, g j ∈ 𝒮 (e j))
    (hgen : Algebra.adjoin (𝒮 0) (Set.range g) = ⊤) {d : ℕ} (hdvd : ∀ j, e j ∣ d) {n : ℕ}
    (b : 𝒮 n) (hkill : ∃ N : ℕ, ∀ m : ℕ, N ≤ m → ∀ y : S, y ∈ 𝒮 (m * d) → y * (b : S) = 0) :
    degreeSection 𝒮 n b = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ := hkill
  refine degreeSection_eq_zero_of_forall_exists_pow_mul_eq_zero 𝒮 g
    (fun j ↦ ⟨e j, he j, hg j⟩)
    (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.iSup_basicOpen_eq_top' 𝒮 g (fun j ↦ ⟨e j, hg j⟩) hgen) b
    fun j ↦ ⟨N * (d / e j), ?_⟩
  have hpow := SetLike.pow_mem_graded (A := 𝒮) (N * (d / e j)) (hg j)
  rw [smul_eq_mul, mul_assoc, Nat.div_mul_cancel (hdvd j)] at hpow
  exact hN N le_rfl _ hpow

/-- **The vanishing criterion for a twisted section over a Noetherian graded ring with generators
of arbitrary positive degrees.** With `d` a common multiple of the degrees of a family of
homogeneous generators of `S` over `𝒮 0`, the canonical section of `𝒪(n)` attached to `b ∈ 𝒮 n`
vanishes exactly when

`𝒮 (m · d) · b = 0 for all m ≫ 0`.

The restriction of the multipliers to the degrees divisible by `d`, and the quantifier "for all
`m ≫ 0`" rather than "for some `m`", are both essential: a single component `𝒮 M` annihilating
`b` says nothing when `S` is not generated in degree one, since `𝒮 (M + k)` need not be contained
in `𝒮 k · 𝒮 M`. -/
theorem degreeSection_eq_zero_iff_forall_mul_eq_zero [IsNoetherianRing S] {ι : Type*}
    (g : ι → S) (e : ι → ℕ) (he : ∀ j, 0 < e j) (hg : ∀ j, g j ∈ 𝒮 (e j))
    (hgen : Algebra.adjoin (𝒮 0) (Set.range g) = ⊤) {d : ℕ} (hd : 0 < d)
    (hdvd : ∀ j, e j ∣ d) {n : ℕ} (b : 𝒮 n) :
    degreeSection 𝒮 n b = 0 ↔
      ∃ N : ℕ, ∀ m : ℕ, N ≤ m → ∀ y : S, y ∈ 𝒮 (m * d) → y * (b : S) = 0 :=
  ⟨exists_forall_mul_eq_zero_of_degreeSection_eq_zero 𝒮 g e he hg hgen hd hdvd b,
    degreeSection_eq_zero_of_forall_mul_eq_zero 𝒮 g e he hg hgen hdvd b⟩

/-! ### The clause: `I(V₊(I))` at the lcm of the degrees of the generators -/

variable (I : HomogeneousIdeal 𝒮)

/-- **The twisted section on `V₊(I) = Proj (𝒮 ⧸ I)` attached to the class of a homogeneous
element `a` of `S` vanishes exactly when `𝒮 (m · d) · a ⊆ I` for all `m ≫ 0`.** The generators of
`S` over `𝒮 0` have the same degrees in the quotient
(`Stacks.HomogeneousIdeal.adjoin_quotientGrading_range_eq_top`), so the same `d` serves there, and
Noetherianness transfers along the surjection. -/
theorem degreeSection_quotientGradingMk_eq_zero_iff_forall_mul_mem [IsNoetherianRing S]
    {ι : Type*} (g : ι → S) (e : ι → ℕ) (he : ∀ j, 0 < e j) (hg : ∀ j, g j ∈ 𝒮 (e j))
    (hgen : Algebra.adjoin (𝒮 0) (Set.range g) = ⊤) {d : ℕ} (hd : 0 < d)
    (hdvd : ∀ j, e j ∣ d) {n : ℕ} (a : 𝒮 n) :
    degreeSection (quotientGrading I) n (quotientGradingMk I n a) = 0 ↔
      ∃ N : ℕ, ∀ m : ℕ, N ≤ m → ∀ y : S, y ∈ 𝒮 (m * d) → y * (a : S) ∈ I.toIdeal := by
  have : IsNoetherianRing (S ⧸ I.toIdeal) :=
    isNoetherianRing_of_surjective S (S ⧸ I.toIdeal) (quotientMk I : S →+* S ⧸ I.toIdeal)
      (surjective_quotientMk I)
  rw [degreeSection_eq_zero_iff_forall_mul_eq_zero (quotientGrading I)
    (fun j ↦ (quotientMk I (g j) : S ⧸ I.toIdeal)) e he
    (fun j ↦ (quotientMk I).map_mem (hg j)) (adjoin_quotientGrading_range_eq_top I g hgen) hd
    hdvd (quotientGradingMk I n a)]
  exact exists_congr fun N ↦ forall_congr' fun m ↦ imp_congr_right fun _ ↦
    forall_mul_quotientGradingMk_eq_zero_iff I a

/-- **Stacks 0BXK for a graded ring that is not generated in degree one: the ideal of equations of
`V₊(I)` is the set of elements that `𝒮 (n · d)` carries into `I` for every `n ≫ 0`**, where `d` is
the least common multiple of the degrees of a finite family of homogeneous generators of `S` over
`𝒮 0`:

`I(V₊(I)) = {x ∈ A | A_{nd} x ⊆ I for all n ≫ 0}`.

An element lies in `I(V₊(I)) = Ker(A ⟶ ⨁_{n ≥ 0} Γ(V₊(I), 𝒪_{V₊(I)}(n)))` exactly when the
twisted section attached to the class of each of its homogeneous components vanishes on
`V₊(I) = Proj (𝒮 ⧸ I)`; both sides of the formula are degreewise conditions, and the finitely
many components are matched by taking the largest of their exponents. -/
@[stacks 0BXK "for `d` the lcm of the degrees of generators of `A` over `A_0`, \
`I(V_+(I)) = {x ∈ A | A_{nd} x ⊂ I for all n ≫ 0}`; `𝒪_{V_+(I)}(n)` is the twisting sheaf of \
`V_+(I) = Proj(A/I)`, the reading in which the source derives this from Cohomology of Schemes \
tag 0BXF applied to `A/I`"]
theorem forall_degreeSection_quotientGradingMk_eq_zero_iff [IsNoetherianRing S] {ι : Type*}
    [Fintype ι] (g : ι → S) (e : ι → ℕ) (he : ∀ j, 0 < e j) (hg : ∀ j, g j ∈ 𝒮 (e j))
    (hgen : Algebra.adjoin (𝒮 0) (Set.range g) = ⊤) (x : S) :
    (∀ n : ℕ, degreeSection (quotientGrading I) n
        (quotientGradingMk I n (decompose 𝒮 x n)) = 0) ↔
      ∃ N : ℕ, ∀ m : ℕ, N ≤ m →
        ∀ y : S, y ∈ 𝒮 (m * Finset.univ.lcm e) → y * x ∈ I.toIdeal := by
  classical
  have hd : 0 < Finset.univ.lcm e := by
    rcases Nat.eq_zero_or_pos (Finset.univ.lcm e) with h | h
    · rw [Finset.lcm_eq_zero_iff] at h
      obtain ⟨j, -, hj⟩ := h
      exact absurd hj (he j).ne'
    · exact h
  have hdvd : ∀ j, e j ∣ Finset.univ.lcm e := fun j ↦ Finset.dvd_lcm (Finset.mem_univ j)
  constructor
  · intro hx
    choose! N hN using fun n ↦ (degreeSection_quotientGradingMk_eq_zero_iff_forall_mul_mem 𝒮 I
      g e he hg hgen hd hdvd (decompose 𝒮 x n)).mp (hx n)
    refine ⟨(decompose 𝒮 x).support.sup N, fun m hm y hy ↦ ?_⟩
    rw [← DirectSum.sum_support_decompose 𝒮 x, Finset.mul_sum]
    exact Ideal.sum_mem _ fun n hn ↦
      hN n m (le_trans (Finset.le_sup hn) hm) y hy
  · rintro ⟨N, hN⟩ n
    refine (degreeSection_quotientGradingMk_eq_zero_iff_forall_mul_mem 𝒮 I g e he hg hgen hd
      hdvd (decompose 𝒮 x n)).mpr ⟨N, fun m hm y hy ↦ ?_⟩
    have h := (Stacks.GradedRing.mul_mem_isHomogeneous_iff_forall_proj 𝒮 I.2 hy x).mp
      (hN m hm y hy) n
    rwa [GradedRing.proj_apply] at h

/-- **The same, as the equality of sets the source displays:**

`I(V₊(I)) = {x ∈ A | A_{nd} x ⊂ I for all n ≫ 0}`. -/
@[stacks 0BXK "for `d` the lcm of the degrees of generators of `A` over `A_0`, \
`I(V_+(I)) = {x ∈ A | A_{nd} x ⊂ I for all n ≫ 0}`; `𝒪_{V_+(I)}(n)` is the twisting sheaf of \
`V_+(I) = Proj(A/I)`, the reading in which the source derives this from Cohomology of Schemes \
tag 0BXF applied to `A/I`"]
theorem setOf_forall_degreeSection_quotientGradingMk_eq_zero [IsNoetherianRing S] {ι : Type*}
    [Fintype ι] (g : ι → S) (e : ι → ℕ) (he : ∀ j, 0 < e j) (hg : ∀ j, g j ∈ 𝒮 (e j))
    (hgen : Algebra.adjoin (𝒮 0) (Set.range g) = ⊤) :
    {x : S | ∀ n : ℕ, degreeSection (quotientGrading I) n
        (quotientGradingMk I n (decompose 𝒮 x n)) = 0} =
      {x : S | ∃ N : ℕ, ∀ m : ℕ, N ≤ m →
        ∀ y : S, y ∈ 𝒮 (m * Finset.univ.lcm e) → y * x ∈ I.toIdeal} :=
  Set.ext fun x ↦ forall_degreeSection_quotientGradingMk_eq_zero_iff 𝒮 I g e he hg hgen x

end AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj

end
